      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=78341090\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 4/5</h2>\n\n**[Medium impact]** Changes condition for using optimized matrix multiplication path\\.\n\nThe PR appears safe to merge, with a non-blocking request to test the newly enabled NVFP4 evaluation path.\n\n<h2>Findings</h2>\n\n1. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**Evaluation path lacks a test** <a href=\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3666#discussion_r4237413434\">▶</a>\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nEnables the single-group NVFP4 FC2 GEMM path when weight gradients are not needed, even without columnwise activation storage.\n- Evaluation can use dense single-group FC2 GEMM.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:4 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Change to enable CuteDSL DenseGEMM for e...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/90e030ac694d570b3bbf1646d6b2668581851ef3) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_expert&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=code_reviews&utm_content=nvidia/transformerengine)</sub>",
